<title>JAPAN: Japan lifts ban on U.S. tomato imports--report.</title>
<headline>Japan lifts ban on U.S. tomato imports--report.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's farm ministry on Thursday announced it had lifted an import ban on 25 kinds of U.S. tomatoes, saying the products had been examined and found free of Tobacco Blue Mold disease, Kyodo news agency reported.</p>
<p>The examination was conducted at the request of the U.S. government, the report said.</p>
<p>No other details of the decision to lift the ban were immediately available.</p>
</text>
